From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eggdogo <eggdogo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:38:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sweet: reduce ZONE_MAP_VA_SIZE to 8GB for 39-bit VA space

On ARMv8.0 devices with 39-bit VA space without ARM_LARGE_MEMORY (such as
MSM8916 / Cortex-A53), the entire kernel_map VA size is 112 GB
(from 0xffffffe000000000 to 0xfffffffbffffffff).
The default macOS ZONE_MAP_VA_SIZE is 128 GB, which exceeds the total
kernel_map size and panics in kmem_range_init() (vm_map_locate_space
failing for claim zones).
Reduce ZONE_MAP_VA_SIZE to 8 GB on SWEET so all kernel zone submaps
and metadata fit comfortably in the 39-bit kernel address space.
---
 osfmk/kern/zalloc.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/zalloc.c b/osfmk/kern/zalloc.c
index 182b44a..2846416 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/zalloc.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/zalloc.c
@@ -160,7 +160,10 @@ ZONE_DEFINE_TYPE(percpu_u64_zone, "percpu.64", uint64_t,
 #define ZONE_GUARD_SPARSE       (64  * 1024)
 #endif /* ZSECURITY_CONFIG(SAD_FENG_SHUI) */
 
-#if XNU_PLATFORM_MacOSX
+#if defined(SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#define ZONE_MAP_MAX            (1ULL << 30)
+#define ZONE_MAP_VA_SIZE        (8ULL << 30)
+#elif XNU_PLATFORM_MacOSX
 #define ZONE_MAP_MAX            (32ULL << 30)
 #define ZONE_MAP_VA_SIZE        (128ULL << 30)
 #else /* XNU_PLATFORM_MacOSX */
-- 
